<& /page/page_title.mas, title => '關於分泌途徑(About Secretory Pathways)' &>

<div class="indented_content" style="width: 80%; margin: 1em auto">

  <p>
     真核細胞蛋白質分泌的主要途徑被稱為經典分泌途徑，或內質網 (ER)／高基氏體依賴型分泌途徑。簡而言之，真核生物分泌蛋白利用 N 端訊息胜肽 (SP) 引導其在 ER 結合核糖體上共轉譯進入 ER 腔，隨後它們穿過內膜系統，最終被輸出到細胞外環境或細胞表面。需要注意的是，這些僅代表含 SP 蛋白質的一個子集，因為其他蛋白質會滯留在 ER 或高基氏體中，或被重新定向到其他細胞區室（例如液泡）。(The primary route for protein secretion from eukaryotic cells is termed the classical, or endoplasmic reticulum (ER)/Golgi-dependent, secretory pathway. Briefly, secreted eukaryotic proteins utilize an N-terminal signal peptide (SP) to direct their co-translation on ER-bound ribosomes into the ER lumen, after which they progress through the endomembrane system and are ultimately exported to the extracellular environment, or cell surface. It should be noted that these represent a subset of SP-containing proteins, since others are retained in the ER or Golgi or are redirected to other compartments, such as the vacuole.)
  </p>

  <div style="width: 500px" class="captioned_image">

    <img src="/documents/img/secretom/classical_secretory_pathway_400.png" />


    <p>
      植物經典分泌途徑的示意圖，突顯了 ER 結合核糖體在 ER 腔中的蛋白質共轉譯易位以及隨後的主要運輸途徑（N，細胞核；ER，內質網；Chl，葉綠體；TGN，反面高基氏體網絡；PVC，前液泡區室；PM，質膜；CW，細胞壁）。改編自 <a href="http://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pubmed/18627574">Foresti and Denecke (2008)</a>。(Schematic diagram of the plant classical secretory pathway, highlighting protein co-translational translocation from ER-bound ribosomes in the ER lumen and the subsequent major trafficking pathways (N, nucleus; ER, endoplasmic reticulum, Chl, chloroplast; TGN, trans-Golgi network; PVC pre-vacuolar compartment; PM, plasma membrane; CW, cell wall). Adapted from <a href="http://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pubmed/18627574">Foresti and Denecke (2008)</a>.)

    </p>

  </div>


  <p>
     越來越多的證據表明，植物蛋白也可以透過獨立於 ER-高基氏體途徑的路徑分泌至質外體。此類蛋白質沒有規範的訊息胜肽，使用破壞 ER 和高基氏體之間囊泡運輸的化學抑制劑（例如布雷菲德菌素 A）進行處理並不會干擾分泌。雖然在<a href="http://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pubmed/16356720">酵母(yeast)</a>和<a href="http://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pubmed/19122676">哺乳動物細胞(mammalian cells)</a>中對此類非經典途徑進行了研究，並且為此類哺乳動物蛋白提供了<a href="http://www.cbs.dtu.dk/services/SecretomeP/">搜尋工具(search tool)</a>，但對植物中此類途徑基本上仍一無所知。這將在該計畫中進行探討。(There is also growing evidence that plant proteins can be secreted to the apoplast via routes that are independent of the ER-Golgi pathway. Such proteins do not have canonical signal peptides and treatment with chemical inhibitors, such as brefeldin A, which disrupt vesicle trafficking between the ER and Golgi, and does not perturb secretion. While such non-classical pathways have been studied in <a href="http://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pubmed/16356720">yeast</a> and <a href="http://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pubmed/19122676">mammalian cells</a>, and a <a href="http://www.cbs.dtu.dk/services/SecretomeP/">search tool</a> is available for such mammalian proteins, essentially nothing is yet known about such pathways in plants. This will be addressed in this project.)
  </p>
</div>
